## Why This Is Asked

This tests practical, beginner-friendly steps to mitigate a known-vulnerability in a gateway without full rewrite, emphasizing token lifecycle, key rotation, and dependency governance.

## Key Concepts

- JWT lifetimes and rotation
- Key management and revocation lists
- Gateway security posture
- Continuous integration security gates

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal token verification middleware (Express)
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
const { getCurrentPublicKey, isRevoked } = require('./security');

function verifyToken(req, res, next) {
  const auth = req.headers.authorization || '';
  const token = auth.split(' ')[1];
  if (!token) return res.status(401).send('Unauthorized');
  try {
    const payload = jwt.verify(token, getCurrentPublicKey(), { algorithms: ['RS256'] });
    if (isRevoked(payload.jti)) return res.status(401).send('Revoked');
    req.user = payload;
    next();
  } catch {
    res.status(401).send('Unauthorized');
  }
}
```

